Ansible Facts:
---------------
-Ansible Facts = auto-collected device data
-stored in ansible_facts variable,
-accessed via dot or bracket notation. 🎯
      Dot notation       → ansible_facts.os_version
      Bracket notation   → ansible_facts['os_version']
-What facts contain:
      - Hardware info
      - IP addresses
      - OS details
      - Network interfaces
      - Software versions
- Facts are used to make dynamic decisions in tasks
- Facts are collected from managed nodes automatically,
  no need to write extra commands

Code:-
=====
---
- name: Gather Ansible Facts              # Play name/description
  hosts: CSR1                             # Target device: CSR1 (Cisco router)
  gather_facts: true                      # Enable automatic fact gathering
  gather_subset: all                      # Collect ALL available facts
  tasks:
    - name: Display Ansible Facts         # Task name
      ansible.builtin.debug:              # Built-in debug module to print output
        msg:
          - "{{ ansible_facts }}"         # Print ALL collected facts (big dictionary)
          - "{{ ansible_facts.net_model }}"  # Print only device model name

Simple Rule :-
        gather_subset: all       →  collect everything
        ansible_facts            →  access everything
        ansible_facts.net_model  →  access specific value 🎯

